# Draft PRs = no checks

Save CI/Vercel until the PR is ready for review.

## Rule

| PR state | GitHub Actions | Vercel Git |
|----------|----------------|------------|
| **draft** | Jobs skipped (`ci.yml` `if`) | No feature-branch deploy (`vercel.json` `**`: false) |
| **ready** | Runs lint/typecheck | Still no feature-branch deploy — preview = `development` / local |
| **push** to `development` | Always runs | `rocha-cotizador-dev` builds; prod project ignore-skips |
| **push** to `main` | Always runs | Auto-deploy off; Actions ships prod |

Belt: `scripts/vercel-ignore-draft-pr.sh` cancels draft / prod-project preview if a deploy still starts.

## Agent behavior

- **Always** open feature/fix PRs as **draft** (`gh pr create --draft`). Default forever unless the user explicitly asks for ready.
- **Never** mark Ready for review yourself — only the user does that manually (triggers CI).
- Do **not** run `gh pr ready` / convert out of draft unless the user ordered it in chat.
- Do **not** add branch-only `deploymentEnabled` hacks that re-enable feature previews without asking.
- While PR is draft: no need to wait on `gh pr checks` (CI/preview skipped).

## Vercel token

Preview env needs `GITHUB_TOKEN` (or `GH_TOKEN`) with `repo` / `pull_requests: read` so the ignore script can see draft status on this private repo. Without it, script **fails closed** (cancels feature-branch builds).

